1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,033
This is Loci, a personal assistant whose memory lives in CockroachDB.

2
00:00:05,050 --> 00:00:09,578
Twelve memories, three sessions, and four open tasks are already here.

3
00:00:09,650 --> 00:00:11,075
Ask what it remembers.

4
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:17,353
Loci embeds the question, runs a cosine vector search, and answers from the memories it retrieves.

5
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:23,997
The trace shows every recalled memory, with its similarity score.

6
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:27,412
The strongest match: Maya, your cofounder.

7
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:35,003
Now start a fresh session and share something new. My sister Nisha is a pediatrician in Boston.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:43,613
A memory writer extracts the durable fact, embeds it, and writes it to CockroachDB. The memory palace updates in place.

9
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:52,067
Open another session and ask about Nisha. There is no local chat history, but the vector index brings her back.

10
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,049
Tasks live in the same database. Ask for one in plain language, and Loci resolves the due date.

11
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:08,115
One durable store holds messages, memories, and tasks.

12
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:16,327
Under the hood, a prefixed distributed vector index scopes recall to this user's live memories before the top-k scan.

13
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:22,291
Loci: the agent that remembers you, built on CockroachDB.
